{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"- **Fund governance:** Establish a registered investment company (typically a trust), board (including independent trustees), officers, governing documents, compliance program/CCO, and written policies. The adviser/sponsor may also provide administration or other services, subject to board oversight and contracts.\n- **Core providers:** Appoint a custodian; fund accountant/administrator; transfer agent; and independent audit firm. Some functions can be bundled with one provider or affiliated entities, with appropriate oversight and conflict controls.\n- **Distribution and operations:** Arrange securities distribution/underwriting (often an affiliate), creation/redemption processing with authorized participants, and basket handling. Select a listing exchange and coordinate with a clearing agency and settlement/depository infrastructure (typically NSCC/DTC).\n- **Strategy-dependent:** A passive ETF needs index rights and an index provider; an active ETF does not necessarily. Securities-lending agent and lending program are optional, not universal. Derivatives, foreign markets, or other specialized strategies may require additional counterparties, documentation, and operational support."}}
